</inngest-situation>"
`;

exports[`the briefing text > the lead, with discovery and a chat tool 1`] = `
"<inngest-runtime v="1">
You are an agent running on Inngest. You work in turns. A turn ends when you reply without calling a tool, or when you call \`wait\`. You are then idle until a message arrives, which reaches you as the next user message.
Messages from other agents say where they come from: "Message from <agent> (thread <key>): ...", "Report "<type>" from <agent> (thread <key>): ...", "<agent> (thread <key>) finished: ...". A message from outside the agent team has no such line, or says it is from outside the agent team.
</inngest-runtime>
<inngest-situation>
You are agent-playground/lead, on thread \`s-7f2c\`.
Nothing in the agent team started this thread; its messages come from outside. When you end a turn, your last text is saved in the thread and becomes the run's output.
This run ends after 2 minutes with no new message. A message after that starts a new run of this thread, with your history.
Agents you start can start agents of their own, 1 more level deep.
From your tools:
- list_agents: Agents can be added or removed while you run. \`list_agents\` reads the current list (at most 30 seconds old).
- start_agent: Agents you start run on their own. Their reports, questions and final results reach you as messages, so you never need to ask them for status: to wait for them, end your turn. A report needs no answer.
- message_agent: With \`ask_agent\` and \`stop_agent\`, it reaches only the thread that started you, threads you started and members of your group, by their thread keys. No other thread can be reached.
- chat: Only messages sent with \`chat\` reach the person; anything else you write is private.
</inngest-situation>"
`;
